    "body": "## Description\n\nAdd a URL bar (a `Gtk::Entry` widget) at the top of the main window. For now, the URL bar is UI-only — typing in it and pressing Enter does nothing. The wiring to actual navigation will come in a later task.\n\n**Depends on:** the refactor task (splitting `main.cpp` into `window.hpp`/`window.cpp`). Do that task first, or coordinate in the issue comments.\n\n## Steps to Complete\n\n1. In `src/browser/window.hpp`, add a `Gtk::Entry` member for the URL bar.\n2. In `src/browser/window.cpp`, replace the current top-level `set_child(m_label)` with a `Gtk::Box` (vertical) containing:\n   - The URL bar at the top.\n   - The existing placeholder label below it.\n3. Configure the URL bar:\n   - Placeholder text: `\"Enter a URL\"`\n   - `set_hexpand(true)` so it stretches horizontally\n   - Small margin around it (e.g., 6 px)\n4. The URL bar does not need to do anything yet.\n5. Rebuild and run. The window should show the URL bar at the top, with the placeholder label below.\n6. Commit with `feat(ui): add URL bar widget`.\n7. Open a pull request.\n\n## Learning Outcomes\n\n- Using `Gtk::Box` for layout in GTK 4.\n- Understanding widget expansion and margins.\n- Working with `Gtk::Entry` (single-line text input).\n\n## Helpful Resources\n\n- [gtkmm4: Gtk::Entry](https://gnome.pages.gitlab.gnome.org/gtkmm/classGtk_1_1Entry.html)\n- [gtkmm4: Gtk::Box](https://gnome.pages.gitlab.gnome.org/gtkmm/classGtk_1_1Box.html)\n",
